===============================================================================

PgPeek has been installed and mounted at /pg_peek.

Next steps:

1. Map your databases to their ActiveRecord classes in
   config/initializers/pg_peek.rb:

     config.connections = { "primary" => "ApplicationRecord" }

   Every database you want to inspect needs an entry, or it will not be listed.

2. Visit /pg_peek to view your PostgreSQL databases

Before deploying:

   pg_peek exposes your schema, every normalized query in the database, and an
   endpoint that resets query statistics. Outside development and test it
   refuses to serve until you say how it is protected.

   Give it credentials, and it will ask for them:

     PG_PEEK_USERNAME=... PG_PEEK_PASSWORD=...

   Or, if you mount it behind authentication you already have, say so in
   config/initializers/pg_peek.rb:

     config.public_dashboard = true

===============================================================================
